course: dictionary
lesson: 7822
title: Meeting a strange fruit in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a new word from the words around it. «An apple's seeds sit in five little rooms arranged in a star, and pears and quinces hide the same star.» Apples and pears are fruits, and quinces sit next to them in the sentence, so a quince is probably a fruit too.
explain: The sentence also tells you that the seeds hide in a star shape. Quinces have seeds in the same star pattern, so you can picture the fruit inside as well as its name. Always ask what word would fit: here, a fruit.
explain: Words in a poem can give clues too. In «The Owl and the Pussycat», the pair «dined on mince, and slices of quince». Food is being eaten, so quince is something people eat. A dictionary tells you the rest: raw quince is hard and sour, but cooked it turns sweet and pink.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A quince is a hard, yellow fruit shaped like a big pear.
fact: Raw quinces are very sour and hard, but cooked quinces are sweet and pink.
fact: Quinces are used to make jam, jelly and paste, such as membrillo, which is often eaten with cheese.
fact: The quince tree grows the fruit, and the ornamental quince is a garden bush with bright red or pink flowers in spring.
exercise: «An apple's seeds sit in five little rooms arranged in a star, and pears and quinces hide the same star.» What is a quince? | A type of bird | A kind of cheese | *A hard, yellow fruit shaped like a big pear | A small pink flower that grows in spring
exercise: Quinces are sour and hard when raw. What makes them sweet and pink? | Painting them | Leaving them in the sun | Freezing them | *Cooking them
exercise: Find and copy the word in «pears and quinces hide the same star» that names a fruit. | hide | star | same | *quinces
test: Quinces are used to make jam, jelly and paste. Which food is membrillo, often eaten with cheese? | Pear juice | Cherry pie | Apple crumble | *Quince paste
test: A garden bush with bright red or pink flowers in spring is called what? | A cheese plant | An apple tree | *An ornamental quince | A pear tree
exam: Which sentence about quinces is true? | They are blue and grow underground | They are a type of cheese that is eaten with jam | They are sweet and soft when raw, like a ripe banana | *They are hard and sour when raw, but sweet and pink when cooked
